{"purpose":"Validate how the EKA AI Skill Pack (skills + commands) must be adjusted for the MCP era, and design a proper agent-agnostic mechanism for command delegation — so eka-discuss/eka-execute and the eka-* skills work identically across agent ecosystems (opencode, Claude Code, Codex, future MCP-driven agents) without hardcoded agent names.","content":"Theme under validation: agent-agnostic skill pack for the MCP era. Context: the skill pack (skills/ tree + commands/ eka-discuss.md + eka-execute.md, embedded in the eka binary, ADR-022/ADR-023) was authored when EKA had no MCP server; commands hardcode opencode agent names in their bodies (alex-architect, alex-backend, althea-product-specialist, etc.) and the frontmatter pins agent: alex. With eka-mcp exposing retrieval primitives today (get/domain/status) and authoring primitives mandated by req:eka-mcp-production (req:eka-mcp-production, approved), the pack must be adjusted: (1) commands must be agent-agnostic — delegation via role-based contracts with a per-ecosystem mapping layer, not hardcoded sub-agent names; (2) skills must be consumable through MCP-era flows, not only via file installation; (3) the boundary stays: commands are agent-layer workflows, MCP exposes primitives only (req:eka-mcp-production locked decision — commands are NOT wrapped as MCP tools). Research questions: what is the proper delegation contract (roles, deliverables, escalation) that any agent runtime can map to its own sub-agents? What happens in ecosystems without sub-agents (single-agent degrade path)? How do skills get installed/loaded across ecosystems (opencode skills dir, claude skills, codex prompts) and does the embedded-pack + eka install model (ADR-023) still hold? Does MCP change how skills are invoked (skills-as-MCP-resources vs file installation)? What is the minimal adjustment that keeps the pack portable and the commands maintainable in one place?","investigationSummary":"Conflict/duplicate check (2026-08-15): no existing knowledge covers agent-agnostic command design. In-force constraints: req:eka-mcp-production (approved) — commands stay agent-layer workflows, MCP exposes primitives only, wrapping eka-discuss/eka-execute as MCP tools is out of scope; ADR-022 (accepted) — skill pack is behavior layer, zero runtime surface, modular skills (one skill per concern), portability by convention (one folder per skill); ADR-023 (accepted) — commands are embedded in the binary, installed via eka install skills/commands with --target opencode|claude, frontmatter is per-provider while bodies claim to be provider-agnostic. Actual state verified from source (eka-mcp repo, 2026-08-15): eka-discuss.md and eka-execute.md both carry frontmatter 'agent: alex' and hardcode opencode agent names in delegation sections (discuss: alex-architect/althea-product-specialist/althea-ux-specialist/explore for analysis, alex-qa/alex-reviewer/althea-review-specialist for review; execute: alex-backend/alex-frontend/alex-devops/alex-documenter/alex-qa/alex-reviewer/alex-security/althea-product-specialist). README acknowledges the mapping burden ('map them to the equivalent sub-agents of the target ecosystem') — manual, per-upgrade. Skills: 11 eka-* skills per manifest.yaml (docs say 10 — a known doc drift, open item), installed by copy; MCP server (eka-mcp v0.1) exposes tools/resources but the skill pack is not yet reachable through MCP. No contradiction found: the theme is additive, research-only, Discovery stratum. Architecture analysis (alex-architect, 2026-08-15): recommended mechanism — (1) role-based delegation contract in command bodies: 9 stable roles (architecture-analysis, product-analysis, ux-analysis, knowledge-discovery, qa-review, technical-review, security-review, product-review, implementer-by-domain:{backend|frontend|devops|docs}) with input/deliverable/escalation contract, never concrete agent names; (2) per-ecosystem mapping layer — mappings/{opencode,claude,codex,default}.md pre-rendered, installed as DELEGATION.md sidecar, installer is pure copy (no parsing); (3) solo-mode degrade path — no sub-agent tool =\u003e primary performs role inline, recorded (mode: solo in checkpoint/final report), never silent; for /eka-execute the hard rule primary-never-implements becomes conditional; (4) canonical command body carries only description frontmatter; provider frontmatter (agent: alex, disable-model-invocation) is rendered by the installer per target; (5) skills: dual path — file install stays primary (ADR-023 model intact) PLUS MCP resources eka://skills and eka://skills/\u003cname\u003e serving SKILL.md content with description from frontmatter (discovery contract preserved); req:eka-mcp-production already lists eka://skills/\u003cname\u003e in its resources; commands are NOT MCP tools (req locked) and NOT MCP resources (out of scope, open question); (6) skill references in command bodies become load-order protocol: installed skill dir first, MCP resource second, else proceed with inline hard rules; (7) command bodies become transport-neutral: primitives cited as CLI and MCP tools as equal paths. Product analysis (althea-product-specialist, 2026-08-15): value ranking — open-standard credibility (c) \u003e new ecosystems Claude/Codex (b) \u003e status-quo opencode (a); nuance: external opencode adopters without alex-* agents also break today; framing: \"one command body, declarative role contract, per-ecosystem mapping\" — not \"works anywhere\"; MVP: both commands, 3 ecosystems (opencode must-not-regress + claude + codex); non-goals: commands as MCP tools (locked), automated per-ecosystem test harness; risks: taxonomy bloat (mitigate: small stable role set derived from actual delegation needs), silent degrade (mitigate: explicit reporting), body vagueness (mitigate: keep specific deliverables per role), opencode regression (mitigate: opencode+maleolabs mapping = default reference, smoke tests); priority: follow-up after mcp-production, same release train as release-coordination; cheap packaging fixes (README -\u003e explicit mapping) can ship anytime; skills consumption: file install sufficient for behavior layer, MCP resources for data/state, transport neutrality is the real MCP-era adjustment. Session decisions (2026-08-15, user): skills = dual path (file install + MCP resources); solo-mode /eka-execute = proceed + record (self-review, weaker assurance, reported); priority = follow-up post mcp-production. Discussion evidence: cmt:agent-agnostic-skill-pack-implementation. Review (2026-08-15): alex-qa PASS WITH FINDINGS (structural valid, 5/5 truthfulness claims verified from source, stratification correct, boundary req:eka-mcp-production honored; findings: F1 — \"ADR-023 intact\" wording contradicted in-force req:eka-mcp-production decision 10 (ADR-023 superseded, eka install removed, install path = eka plugin install mcp -\u003e eka-mcp install \u003ckind\u003e), FIXED; F2 — skill count 11 vs 10, FIXED; F3 — eka-mcp authoring primitives not yet implemented, FIXED; F4 — cmt publish ordering after fnd, sequencing respected); alex-reviewer PASS WITH FINDINGS (technical mechanism sound; medium findings FIXED: DELEGATION.md would surface as ghost /delegation command in opencode/claude command dirs -\u003e non-.md sidecar name; transport-neutral dual inline citation would bloat body + cite nonexistent authoring tools -\u003e single primitive table in preflight, gated to mcp-production; execute step 5 UX review had no taxonomy role -\u003e product-review contract absorbs UX review; low findings FIXED: product-review agent-shift migration note, solo-mode self-review declaration + checkpoint mode field, Codex solo assumption verification, version drift single-source (pack.go), req resource-list verification item). Discussion evidence: cmt:agent-agnostic-skill-pack-implementation (role implementation, author Marij Mokoginta).","conclusion":"VALIDATED. The skill pack must be adjusted for the MCP era; the mechanism is role-based delegation with a per-ecosystem mapping layer and an explicit solo-mode degrade path. Concrete: (1) command bodies (eka-discuss, eka-execute) drop all hardcoded agent names and frontmatter agent pinning — bodies name the 9 stable roles with input/deliverable/escalation contracts (product-review contract explicitly covers holistic product/UX review — execute step 5 mentions UX review per item class and ux-analysis is analysis-only, so product-review absorbs UX-review to keep the taxonomy at 9 roles); canonical body carries only description; (2) a mappings/ directory ships pre-rendered role-\u003eagent tables per ecosystem (opencode with maleolabs agents = default reference; claude; codex and default = all self/solo (Codex single-agent assumption to be verified against current Codex docs at implementation time; opencode without the maleolabs agent set falls to default.md solo mapping — explicit in README)); installer copies the matching table as a non-.md sidecar (e.g. DELEGATION.txt — opencode and Claude Code legacy command dirs scan every *.md as a command, so DELEGATION.md would surface as a ghost /delegation command) — ecosystem adaptation is declarative, no body editing, no drift; (3) solo mode is explicit: no sub-agent capability =\u003e primary performs roles inline; /eka-discuss degrades benignly, /eka-execute proceeds with primary implementing in the worktree (isolation rules still apply) and records mode: solo in the checkpoint format and declares in the final report that QA/review are self-review (no author-separation gate exists in the runtime — one identity writes both implementation and review notes; weaker assurance, explicitly reported, never silent); (4) skills: dual path — file installation stays the primary delivery (install path per req:eka-mcp-production decision 10: eka plugin install mcp then eka-mcp install \u003ckind\u003e; ADR-023 superseded — the pack is embedded in eka-mcp, not the CLI) and the pack becomes reachable as MCP resources (eka://skills index + eka://skills/\u003cname\u003e with frontmatter descriptions), matching what req:eka-mcp-production already lists; commands stay agent-layer workflows and are never MCP tools (req locked); (5) command bodies become transport-neutral via a single primitive table in preflight (primitive -\u003e CLI command \u003c-\u003e MCP tool), bodies cite primitive names once — not dual inline citation (would bloat the body and would cite authoring tools that do not exist yet; MCP tool citations gated to the mcp-production milestone, reality-check extended: verify the tool table exists before citing); skill references use a load-order protocol (installed skill dir, then MCP resource, else inline hard rules — commands keep working without skills); (6) versioning: pack manifest bump policy extended — role vocabulary changes are breaking bumps, adding a new ecosystem mapping is additive (not breaking); one authoritative version source needed (pack.go, synced to manifest.yaml + anvil.yaml — drift exists today: manifest 0.3.1 vs pack.go 0.1.1); version coupling via embedding stays (in eka-mcp); (7) installer: render frontmatter per target + copy mapping; plugin contract gets additive Target option (backward compatible). Priority: follow-up after mcp-production, same release train as release-coordination; packaging cleanup (README mapping, manifest skill-count sync 11 vs 10) can ship anytime. Out of scope: commands as MCP tools (locked by req:eka-mcp-production), commands as MCP resources (open question, revisit later), per-user mapping override (substitution fallback covers), automated per-ecosystem harness. Open items: (1) migration checklist — /eka-execute today uses althea-product-specialist for product review while /eka-discuss Gate 4 uses althea-review-specialist; role unification makes product-review resolve to ONE mapping row, so the execute behavior shifts — confirm intent during implementation; (2) verify opencode frontmatter-optionality (is agent: required?) before finalizing render logic; (3) verify Claude Code command-dir scan behavior for the sidecar (non-.md name avoids scan; verify empirically); (4) confirm owner of frontmatter rendering (CLI vs plugin) at requirement time — note eka-cli has no top-level eka install today (only eka plugin install); (5) skills transport-neutral note per skill (one-line: CLI equivalents via MCP tools) — not a rewrite; (6) sync docs: manifest lists 11 skills, docs say 10 (eka-feedback); (7) verify req:eka-mcp-production resource list (eka://skills/\u003cname\u003e) before implementation — if absent, amend fnd + req together. Next step per priority: fnd stays research-only; requirement (scp/req) + container prepared after mcp-production, riding release-coordination."}